{"id":"xdg-user-dir.1","n":"xdg-user-dir","s":"1","src":{"r":{"pkg":"xdg-user-dirs","ver":"0.17-10.el9","repo":"AppStream","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/AppStream/x86_64/os/Packages/x/xdg-user-dirs-0.17-10.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man1/xdg-user-dir.1.gz","sha256":"af7fa1b02fd48e314a1b914f7d7fba26f66724cc04edfa702c9ef98296a344b5","date":"","origin":"XDG"},"u":{"pkg":"xdg-user-dirs","ver":"0.17-2ubuntu4","repo":"jammy/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/x/xdg-user-dirs/xdg-user-dirs_0.17-2ubuntu4_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man1/xdg-user-dir.1.gz","sha256":"06c1cb52d3b249aa4b74da0b9fe17c6bfe9b66c3df47e7f7252af14d2a770ce6","date":"","origin":"XDG"}},"nopt":{"r":0,"u":0},"desc":"Find an XDG user dir","same":true,"doc":[["NAME","<p>xdg-user-dir - Find an XDG user dir</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>xdg-user-dir</b> [NAME]</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>xdg-user-dir</b> looks up the current path for one of the special XDG user dirs.</p> <p>This command expects the name of an XDG user dir as argument. The possible names are:</p> <div class=\"in\">DESKTOP</div> <div class=\"in\">DOWNLOAD</div> <div class=\"in\">TEMPLATES</div> <div class=\"in\">PUBLICSHARE</div> <div class=\"in\">DOCUMENTS</div> <div class=\"in\">MUSIC</div> <div class=\"in\">PICTURES</div> <div class=\"in\">VIDEOS</div>"],["FILES","<p>The values are looked up in the user-dirs.dir file. This file is created by the xdg-user-dirs-update utility.</p>"],["ENVIRONMENT","<p>The <b>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</b> environment variable determines where the user-dirs.dirs file is located.</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>xdg-user-dirs-update</b>(1)</p>"]]}